---
description: Coordinate customer onboarding through approved outcomes, evidenced environment fit, dependency planning, measured progress and consented replanning.
args:{request:CustomerLaunchRequest;implementation:CustomerImplementationFile;prior?:OnboardingCheckpoint|null}
returns:OnboardingProgramResult
---
1. Bind saved = prior when supplied, otherwise null. Bind goal = frameLaunch(request, implementation.onboardingRecords) and policy = selectGoverningTerms(request, implementation.governingTerms). Keep customer authority, agreed scope, exclusions, contractual target and internal launch target separate. Bind outcomes = confirmCustomerOutcomes(goal, policy, implementation.onboardingRecords, implementation.evidencePages). A broad aspiration without an owner and observable acceptance remains uncommitted.
2. Bind ownership = transferDepartedOwner(request, implementation.accountTransferReceipts, outcomes). Successor assignment and former administrator credential revocation require separate evidence. Bind environment = mapOnboardingEnvironment(goal, policy, outcomes, implementation.evidencePages). Verify architecture, access classification and sample interface behavior; request approved evidence, never production credentials.
3. Bind productionCheck = compareProductionSample(request, implementation.productionSampleComparisons), fallback = routeUnavailableIntegration(request, implementation.integrationFallbackApprovals), operatorCheck = verifyTaskOperators(request, implementation.operatorCapabilityEvidence), and dates = trackContractAndTargetDates(request, implementation.contractualDateAmendments). Evaluate these independent findings even while discovery is blocked, so changed ownership or contractual dates remain visible. A fallback needs an owner, data boundary, expiry and customer approval; the original integration remains incomplete.
4. Initialize plan = null, progress = null and replan = null. If accepted outcomes have named customer authority and environment compatibility is established, bind plan = constructOutcomeTaskPlan(goal, policy, outcomes, environment, implementation.evidencePages). Require an acyclic dependency path, shared prerequisites once and reversible pilots before broad changes. Use ownership's actual transfer and revocation findings to block dependent tasks; do not ask for a second ownership judgment. Production-check failures block bulk import and operator-check failures block the corresponding tasks.
5. When plan exists, bind progress = measureEvidenceBackedProgress(goal, plan, implementation.evidencePages) for the whole task set. Missing evidence leaves a task pending or attempted, never absent from the ledger. An attempted migration is not reconciled migration and attendance is not demonstrated operator capability.
6. When plan and progress exist and evidence establishes a dependency failure or customer scope change, bind replan = replanOnboardingDependencies(goal, plan, progress, implementation.evidencePages). Preserve accepted work, reopen affected descendants, disclose effort/date consequences and require approval for material changes. Otherwise retain null replan.
7. Bind guardrails = [ownership, productionCheck, fallback, operatorCheck, dates]. Bind unresolved to actual outcome authority/acceptance gaps, environment.unknownInterfaces, environment.securityBlockers, environment.sampleProductionRisks, each guardrail's blockers, and existing plan.blockedOutcomes or progress.residualWork. Bind actions to the guardrails' proposedActions plus evidence-request or customer-review actions supported by these unresolved facts. An execution action stays conditional on its domain gates.
8. Bind checkpoint = reconcileOnboardingCheckpoint(saved, request, implementation, outcomes, plan, progress, replan, ownership, dates). Return { caseId: request.caseId, outcomes, environment, plan, progress, replan, guardrails, unresolved, actions, checkpoint, commitAllowed: false } as OnboardingProgramResult on both discovery and execution-planning paths. Readiness does not assert customer acceptance or completed migration.
